ames>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dutasteride (Avodart) for benign prostatic hyperplasia</article-title><source>Med Lett Drug Ther</source><year>2002</year><volume>44</volume><fpage>109</fpage><lpage>110</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b9-cia-4-251"><label>9.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bramson</surname><given-names>HN</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Unique preclinical characteristics of GG745, a potent dual inhibitor of 5AR</article-title><source>J Pharmacol Exp Ther</source><year>1997</year><volume>282</volume><fpage>1946</fpage><lpage>1502</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b10-cia-4-251"><label>10.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Roehrborn</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Efficacy and safety of a dual inhibitor of 5-alpha-reductase types 1 and 2 (dutasteride) in men with benign prostatic hyperplasia</article-title><source>Urol</source><year>2002</year><volume>60</volume><fpage>434</fpage><lpage>441</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12350480</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b11-cia-4-251"><label>11.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><article-title>AVODART (dutasteride): Prescribing information</article-title><source>Physicians&#x02019; Desk Reference</source><edition>58th ed</edition><publisher-loc>Montvale, NJ</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Thompson PDR</publisher-name><year>2004</year><fpage>1456</fpage><lpage>1459</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12-cia-4-251"><label>12.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Roehrborn</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Long-term sustained improvement in symptoms of benign prostatic hyperplasia with the dual 5&#x003b1;-reductase inhibitor dutasteride: results of 4-year studies</article-title><source>BJU Int</source><year>2005</year><volume>96</volume><fpage>572</fpage><lpage>577</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16104912</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13-cia-4-251"><label>13.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schulman</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Long-term therapy with dual 5&#x003b1;-reductase inhibitor dutasteride is well tolerated in men with symptomatic benign prostatic hyperplasia</article-title><source>BJU Int</source><year>2006</year><volume>97</volume><fpage>73</fpage><lpage>79</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16336332</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14-cia-4-251"><label>14.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>O&#x02019;Leary</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Improvements in benign prostatic hyperplasia-specific quality of life with dutasteride, the novel dual 5&#x003b1;-reductase inhibitor</article-title><source>BJU Int</source><year>2003</year><volume>92</volume><fpage>262</fpage><lpage>266</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12887480</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b15-cia-4-251"><label>15.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Desgrandchamps</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Effect of dutasteride on the symptoms of benign prostatic hyperplasia, and patient quality of life and discomfort in clinical practice</article-title><source>BJU Int</source><year>2006</year><volume>98</volume><fpage>83</fpage><lpage>88</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16831149</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b16-cia-4-251"><label>16.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bostwick</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Does finasteride alter the pathology of the prostate and cancer grading</article-title><source>Clin Prostate Cancer</source><year>2004</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>228</fpage><lpage>235</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15072606</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b17-cia-4-251"><label>17.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gomella</surname><given-names>LG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Chemoprevention using dutasteride: The Reduce Trial</article-title><source>Curr Opin Urol</source><year>2005</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>29</fpage><lpage>32</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15586026</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b18-cia-4-251"><label>18.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Merrick</surname><given-names>GS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Efficacy of neoadjuvant bicalutamide and dutasteride as a cytoreductive regimen before prostate brachytherapy</article-title><source>Urol</source><year>2006</year><volume>68</volume><fpage>116</fpage><lpage>120</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16844453</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b19-cia-4-251"><label>19.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Narayan</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Long-term efficacy and safety of tamsulosin for benign prostatic hyperplasia</article-title><source>Rev Urol</source><year>2005</year><volume>7</volume><issue>Supp 4</issue><fpage>S42</fpage><lpage>S48</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16986054</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b20-cia-4-251"><label>20.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McConnell</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The long-term effect of doxazosinzocin, finasteride, and combination therapy on the clinical progression of benign prostatic hyperplasia</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><year>2003</year><volume>349</volume><fpage>2449</fpage><lpage>2451</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14681512</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b21-cia-4-251"><label>21.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Roehrborn</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The effects of dutasteride, tamsulosin and combination therapy on lower urinary tract symptoms in men with benign prostatic hyperplasia and prostatic enlargement: 2-year results from the CombAT study</article-title><source>J Urol</source><year>2008</year><volume>179</volume><fpage>616</fpage><lpage>621</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18082216</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="f1-cia-4-251" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Dutasteride chemical structure.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="cia-4-251f1"/></fig><fig id="f2-cia-4-251" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Tamulosin chemical structure.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="cia-4-251f2"/></fig><table-wrap id="t1-cia-4-251" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Pharmacokinetics of dutasteride</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Bioavailability</bold></th><th valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>60%</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Steady state</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3 months</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Peak serum concentration</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2&#x02013;3 hours</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Volume of distribution</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">511 L</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Elimination half-life</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5 weeks</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t2-cia-4-251" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Sexual adverse events from dutasteride efficacy and safety study</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Adverse event</bold></th><th valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Placebo</bold></th><th valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Dutasteride</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Impotence</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4.00%</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">7.30%</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Decreased libido</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.10%</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4.20%</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Gynecomastia</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.70%</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.30%</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Ejaculation disorder</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.80%</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.20%</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t3-cia-4-251" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>Pharmacokinetics of tamsulosin</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Bioavailability</bold></th><th valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>90%</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Steady state</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5 days</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Peak serum concentration</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4&#x02013;6 hours</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Volume of distribution</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">16 L</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Elimination half-life</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">15 hours</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap></floats-group></article>